precedence, highest first

  primary         f(x)  a[i]  (e)  T(x)         left
  postfix         .  ?.  ?  !  |>               left
  prefix          !  -  any spelling            right
  user-8                                        left
  multiplication  *  /  %                       left
  user-7                                        left
  addition        +  -                          left
  user-6                                        left
  bitwise         &  |  ^                       left
  user-5          an unrecognised spelling      left
  shift           <<  >>  >>>                   left
  user-4                                        left
  range           ..  ::  ..<  ::<              left
  user-3                                        left
  relational      ==  !=  =~  !~  <  <=  >  >=  left
  user-2                                        left
  boolean         /\  \/                        left
  user-1          ??                            right

the grouping the parser chose

  a +++ b *** c   (a +++ (b *** c))
  a <+> b +++ c   (a <+> (b +++ c))
  a +++ b +++ c   ((a +++ b) +++ c)
  a ?+ b ?+ c     (a ?+ (b ?+ c))
  a <*> b *** c   (a <*> (b *** c))

the same expression, under @precedence

  a <*> b *** c   ((a <*> b) *** c)

arguments are passed by value

  callee wrote a field         99
  callee reassigned the value  1
  callee wrote through a ref   99
